From: ryoma-89 <ryoma-89@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:07:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] gfxstream: answer fence queries from the host's completion
 table

Velox-local change (biblioklept). With debug.velox.fence_shared=1 the
driver reads the fence completion table the Velox host keeps in the ASG
ring page (host gfxstream patch 0021). vkGetFenceStatus and
vkWaitForFences return VK_SUCCESS without a round trip only when the slot
holds this fence's host handle and the reset epoch the guest expects (the
number of vkResetFences it issued, counted before the reset is sent).
Torn slots, foreign handles, missing tables, external (sync fd) fences and
devices with maintenance5 (device loss must reach fence calls) use the
RPC as before. The table pointer is looked up once per thread.

